    @section i18nquickstart Quick Example

    @code{.py}
%requires i18n

printf("%s\n", I18n::plural_category(2, "ru"));
printf("%s\n", I18n::format_percent("0.125", "de-DE"));
printf("%s\n", I18n::format_currency("12.5", "USD", "en-US"));

hash<auto> catalog_data = I18n::load_native_catalog("catalog.json");
I18n::MessageCatalog catalog(catalog_data);
printf("%s\n", catalog.t("Hello, {name}", "cs-CZ", {"name": "Petr"}));
    @endcode

    @section i18nnul Strings with NUL Characters

    Text is processed whole, including any NUL characters: strings to format, compare, search, sort, parse or
    convert, plural forms, function words, and catalog messages, sources and placeholder values.  A number given
    as a string with a NUL character is a malformed number.

    A string that names something cannot contain a NUL character, as it would be cut at the NUL character and name
    something else; such a string is refused with the error that the API raises for an invalid value of that
    string: locales, \c Accept-Language headers, currency codes, string predicate operators, option values naming a
    style, skeleton, plural type or collation strength, catalog domains and paths, and the symbolic message ids
    and message states of message catalogs.  A message catalog looks up a source string used as its own message id
    as text: with a NUL character, it matches no message and is returned as it is.

    @section i18nscope Current Scope

    This module is the implementation target for issue #5334. Rich message formatting, request-locale
    propagation helpers, and machine-translation workflow support are planned follow-up phases in the
    same issue.

